    "body": "Reported by the contributor while testing #482 on a macOS release build (2026-11-09).\n\n**What happens:** the browser tree's row text (Setup, Setups, WCS, Stock, Machine, Fixtures, the Operations rows, Models, Tools) is drawn in a pale grey on the near-white panel. The contrast is very low, and the contributor called it \"REALLY hard to read\". The properties pane on the same panel colour is legible; only the tree rows are washed out. It looks like the tree uses a dimmed or weak text colour tuned for the dark theme, while the panel fill is the light theme's.\n\n**Expected:** the tree's row text meets the same contrast as the properties text in every theme. Muted parts like suffixes and hidden rows may be dimmer, but must still pass a contrast check, as the light theme's other colours already do.\n\n**Done means:** a structural test asserts the tree row text colour against the panel fill passes the same contrast threshold the theme table already checks, in both themes. The tree is readable on the light panel.",
